{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And YHWH was with Joseph.</b> To deliver him from those who rose against him." "<b>And he was a successful man.</b> One who attains every end directed by him." "<b>And he was in the house of his master, the Egyptian.</b> Stationed to serve in his master's chamber. The verb היה has here the sense of עמד (was stationed), as in וְהָיָה שָׁם (Deuteronomy 31:26) and וַיִּהְיוּ שָׁם כַּאֲשֶׁר צִוַּנִי ה׳ (Deuteronomy 10:5)."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:54.149774831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}